WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:04.080
For a long, long time I didn’t know what
was happening to the cows and the chickens

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:06.090
and the dairy and egg industry.

00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:11.059
So once I learned that they forcibly impregnate
the cows, take their babies away, kill the

00:00:11.059 --> 00:00:15.670
bulls, exploit the mothers for five years
until they kill them, grinding up male chickens…so

00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:17.740
there’s a lot of injustice in there.

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:22.480
So once I learned that, I said okay I am a
hypocrite saying I love animals but still

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:23.590
consuming those products.

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:27.470
So that’s when I went vegan four years ago.

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:30.700
We show videos from the international animal
agriculture.

00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:36.230
Doesn’t matter if its organic or factory
farming because it’s always an animal.

00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:39.180
These are videos from all over the world,
even from Germany.

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:45.629
So regularly we just let the people see or
watch the documentaries for 30 seconds, then

00:00:45.629 --> 00:00:53.989
we speak to them and we ask them questions,
to really think about it, to take a breath

00:00:53.989 --> 00:00:55.370
and maybe then talk.

00:00:55.370 --> 00:00:59.850
Because these are very hard documentaries,
and no one wants to see it but everyone wants

00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:00.960
to eat it.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:04.850
You aren’t going to talk to someone who
never thought about veganism and get them

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:06.219
vegan in a second.

00:01:06.219 --> 00:01:10.610
You are just going to plant a seed and then
the next person or the next video they see,

00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:15.689
will put a bit of water on that seed and at
the end, the plant of veganism grows.

00:01:15.689 --> 00:01:20.079
So we can be the last person that talks to
them that makes them go vegan, or the first

00:01:20.079 --> 00:01:24.369
view of animal killings that they see in their
lives.

00:01:24.369 --> 00:01:29.340
Some people might criticize that we are hiding
ourselves behind the mask, but the concept

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:35.409
is, first, the meaning of V for Vendetta,
which is about uncovering injustices and fighting

00:01:35.409 --> 00:01:36.680
against it.

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:42.970
The second reason is that when you go up to
a cube of truth and watch the videos, it’s

00:01:42.970 --> 00:01:45.230
better for you not to feel observed.

00:01:45.230 --> 00:01:52.009
So when someone is wearing the mask, you don’t
feel like he is judging me or gauging my facial

00:01:52.009 --> 00:01:55.990
reactions so it makes it easier for people
to watch the videos.

00:01:55.990 --> 00:02:01.600
I just came from there and I saw them all
wearing these masks.

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:07.249
First of all it’s cool, it absolutely attracted
my attention.

00:02:07.249 --> 00:02:15.510
I just had a really nice conversation with
that dude there, we talked about is that really

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:19.970
human to kill animals and we shared our different
opinions.

00:02:19.970 --> 00:02:27.810
I think it’s good because normally when
you are working in your normal life you don’t

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:31.549
think about these questions that often, or
that deep.

00:02:31.549 --> 00:02:34.760
Because eating meat for us is too normal.

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:37.970
The question I always ask at the beginning
is: What do you think?

00:02:37.970 --> 00:02:39.760
What are your feelings about that?”

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:43.909
And I always specify that there is no right
or wrong answer to that question.

00:02:43.909 --> 00:02:48.360
And then I always say, “Ok so are you against
animal cruelty or do you not like that people

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:49.360
harm the animals?”

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:50.790
And everyone says, “No I do not like that.”

00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:54.580
And then I say, “But do you pay every day
for the people that do that?”

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:56.400
And they say, “Yes, that’s a point.”

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:58.989
And I’m saying like yeah, it’s not about
judging people.

00:02:58.989 --> 00:03:02.791
It’s just about making them realize and
connect the fact that they are paying for

00:03:02.791 --> 00:03:06.489
people to do what they don’t like to see
the people do.

00:03:06.489 --> 00:03:17.640
She told us about the vegans, the violence
against animals, and the torture and the big

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:18.640
animal factories.

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:19.640
We could make an idea about all this.

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:23.120
And we had a small talk about to be vegan
for one week.

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:29.170
I am not vegan now, so I’ll try it for one
week and yeah.

00:03:29.170 --> 00:03:33.590
Being vegan on my own wasn’t enough for
me.

00:03:33.590 --> 00:03:40.480
Because I realized that it’s a good step
to do something yourself, but I want to spread

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:44.590
information to more people in a nice way.

00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:45.590
Not getting angry or so.

00:03:45.590 --> 00:03:51.720
Sometimes in my own environment people get
kind of aggressive when you tell them you’re

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:54.800
vegan, and they get a bad conscious.

00:03:54.800 --> 00:04:03.080
Here it is a good way to get positive information
and to spread something which is maybe contributing

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:04.599
to a better world.

